\par\par \uc2 Business/Financial Desk; SECTB\par \b \uc2 California Cuts Off Walgreens Over Stance on  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Pill\b0\par\par\uc2 By Katie Robertson \par \uc2 411 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 March 2023\par \uc2 The New York Times\par \uc2 NYTF\par \uc2 Late Edition - Final\par 3\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 The New York Times Company.  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 The state will not renew a multimillion-dollar deal, Gov. \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2  said, after the chain announced it would stop distributing mifepristone in 21 states.\par \par \uc2 The governor of California said on Wednesday that he would not renew a multimillion-dollar contract with \uc2 Walgreens\uc2 , after the pharmacy chain announced that it would stop selling an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill in 21 states that had threatened legal action.\par \par \uc2 The governor, \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2 , a Democrat, said he had directed the \uc2 California Department of General Services\uc2  to notify \uc2 Walgreens\uc2  that it would withdraw a planned renewal of the contract that was supposed to take effect on May 1. He said the state had paid \uc2 Walgreens\uc2  $54 million over the life of the contract, which allowed it to get specialty prescription drugs that were mostly used by the Department of Corrections and Rehabilitation.\par \par \uc2 ''California will not stand by as corporations cave to extremists and cut off critical access to reproductive care and freedom,'' Mr. Newsom said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 Walgreens\uc2  has found itself in the middle of the intense political and legal debate over \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights since the Supreme Court last year overturned Roe v. Wade, the 1973 decision that established a federal constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . After Republican attorneys general in 21 states threatened legal action against pharmacy chains that sold the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill mifepristone, \uc2 Walgreens\uc2  said it would no longer distribute the drug in those states.\par \par \uc2 The pharmacy chain's decision was met with instant backlash from some customers and politicians in Democratic-led states. Mr. Newsom said on Monday that California would stop doing business with \uc2 Walgreens\uc2  and that he had ordered a review of all of the state's contracts with the company.\par \par \uc2 Fraser Engerman, a spokesman for \uc2 Walgreens\uc2 , said in an email on Wednesday that the company was ''deeply disappointed'' by California's decision ''not to renew our longstanding contract due to false and misleading information.''\par \par \uc2 ''\uc2 Walgreens\uc2  is facing the same circumstances as all retail pharmacies, and no other retail pharmacies have said that they would approach this situation differently, so it's unclear where this contract would now be moved,'' he said.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Engerman said the company's position had always been to sell the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill where it was legally allowed to do so.\par \par \uc2 ''We will dispense this medication consistent with federal and state laws,'' he added.\par \par \uc2 This article appeared in print on page B3. \par \par \uc2 Document NYTF000020230309ej390004v\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw284\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal4260\pichgoal600
